libslic3r: skip GCode::append_full_config in the BBL branch only

Both GCode::_do_export branches (BBL and non-BBL) originally called
append_full_config unconditionally to dump every print config option as
a `; key = value` comment block. On Android with no preset bundle
loaded, one of the enum config options had a null name table and
ConfigOptionEnumsGenericTempl<false>::serialize_single_value
null-derefs.

Status as of 2026-05-12 (PEGGY-DBG):
  * The non-BBL branch is the only branch OrcaXR ever takes — slic3r_jni
    .cpp forces `print.is_BBL_printer() = false` before _do_export.
  * `fixup_enum_keys_map(cfg)` runs at slice time and re-attaches the
    runtime keys_map pointer to every ConfigOptionEnumsGeneric instance,
    so serialize_single_value no longer null-derefs.
  * Real bundled profiles are loaded via OrcaProfileLoader on Kotlin
    side and threaded into the slice config, so there's a full preset
    chain to serialize.

Net effect: the non-BBL `append_full_config` is now safe AND load-bearing —
without it the emitted CONFIG_BLOCK contains only the first_layer_*
SoftFever scalars and downstream tools (including OrcaXR's own 3MF
re-import path and the user's desktop FullSpectrum gcode-diff baseline)
can't recover keys like `mixed_filament_definitions`, `filament_colour`,
`layer_height`, `dithering_local_z_mode`, etc.

The BBL branch (is_BBL_printer()==true) stays disabled because we never
exercise it and don't want a surprise crash if some other code path
flips the flag.

Retire-if: a `Print` instance ever legitimately needs the BBL gcode
header (BBS-format 3MF roundtrip via libslic3r's own slicer surface);
re-enable the BBL branch then.

---
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp b/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
index fe10cbcd41..2fbad6ea1f 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/GCode.cpp
@@ -2571,8 +2571,13 @@ void GCode::_do_export(Print& print, GCodeOutputStream &file, ThumbnailsGenerato
     {
         if (is_bbl_printers) {
             file.write("; CONFIG_BLOCK_START\n");
+            // OrcaXR: append_full_config crashes on Android when no preset
+            // bundle is loaded — some enum option's name table is null and
+            // serialize_single_value derefs it. Skip the BBL-branch config
+            // dump; OrcaXR forces is_BBL_printer()=false so this branch is
+            // dead code in our pipeline anyway.
             std::string full_config;
-            append_full_config(print, full_config);
+            // append_full_config(print, full_config);
             if (!full_config.empty())
                 file.write(full_config);

